      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Multi-Magnification Attention Fusion for Resource-Efficient Breast Cancer Classification with Integrated Grad-CAM Visualization",
      "year": "2025",
      "subtitle": "Unpublished paper",
      "description": "This study develops a lightweight multi-magnification framework for clinical breast cancer classification, using depthwise separable convolutions and cross-magnification attention. Evaluated on BreakHis, it achieved 93.78% accuracy with 98% fewer parameters than traditional methods and 8.35ms inference time. The framework integrates interpretable Grad-CAM visualizations, enabling effective real-time screening in resource-constrained environments.",
